        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9fb6f607-3ff8-5d5e-9d9c-f2eb2121ee6d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eric Musselman, Bill Musselman, Chuck Daly, Doc Rivers, Lon Kruger, Yanni Hufnagel\n- Organizations: Continental Basketball Association, Minnesota Timberwolves, Orlando Magic, Atlanta Hawks, Detroit Pistons, United States men's Olympic basketball team, Nevada Wolf Pack men's basketball team\n- Events: 1989 NBA Finals, 1990 NBA Finals, 1992 Summer Olympics, 1997–98 Orlando Magic season\n\nFacts:\n- Chuck Daly was an American basketball head coach born on July 20, 1930, and he died on May 9, 2009.\n- Chuck Daly led the Detroit Pistons to consecutive NBA championships in 1989 and 1990.\n- Chuck Daly coached the 1992 United States men's Olympic basketball team, known as the Dream Team, to a gold medal at the 1992 Summer Olympics.\n- Before becoming an NBA assistant coach, Eric Musselman was a head coach in the Continental Basketball Association.\n- Eric Musselman is the son of former NBA head coach Bill Musselman.\n- Eric Musselman later served as an assistant coach with the Minnesota Timberwolves, the Orlando Magic under Chuck Daly and Doc Rivers, and the Atlanta Hawks under Lon Kruger.\n- In the 1997–98 Orlando Magic season, the Orlando Magic hired Chuck Daly as head coach.\n- Yanni Hufnagel last served as an assistant coach for the Nevada Wolf Pack men's basketball team under Eric Musselman.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8028bcd8-5150-5050-be7b-ef26f860833a",
        "text": "Page: Eric Musselman. Sentence: The son of former NBA head coach Bill Musselman, Eric Musselman was a head coach in the Continental Basketball Association (CBA) before becoming an assistant coach with the Minnesota Timberwolves, Orlando Magic (under Chuck Daly and Doc Rivers), and Atlanta Hawks (under Lon Kruger).\nPage: Chuck Daly. Sentence: Charles Jerome Daly (July 20, 1930 – May 9, 2009) was an American basketball head coach.\nPage: Chuck Daly. Sentence: He led the Detroit Pistons to consecutive National Basketball Association (NBA) Championships in 1989 and 1990, and the 1992 United States men's Olympic basketball team (\"The Dream Team\") to the gold medal at the 1992 Summer Olympics.\nPage: Yanni Hufnagel. Sentence: He last served as an assistant coach of the Nevada Wolf Pack men's basketball team under Eric Musselman.\nPage: 1997–98 Orlando Magic season. Sentence: The Magic hired Chuck Daly as head coach, who won two championships coaching the Detroit Pistons.",
